      HOWDOMINO
⌹ IS DOMINO, THE MATRIX DIVIDE. ⌹M IS THE INVERSE OF A SQUARE
MATRIX M, AND B⌹A SOLVES THE EQUATIONS A+.×X=B FOR X, WHICH IS
(⌹A)+.×B WITHOUT FORMING THE INVERSE. B MAY BE A VECTOR, OR A
MATRIX WITH ONE RIGHT-HAND SIDE PER COLUMN.

WHEN A HAS MORE ROWS THAN COLUMNS THE EQUATIONS CANNOT ALL
HOLD, AND B⌹A GIVES THE X THAT MAKES THE SUM OF SQUARED
ERRORS LEAST: THE LEAST SQUARES FIT, WHICH IS HOW STATS
FITS A LINE. A SINGULAR A IS A DOMAIN ERROR.

      ⌹2 2⍴4 7 2 6
 0.6 ¯0.7
¯0.2  0.4
      HOWDET
DET M WORKS THE DETERMINANT OUT BY ELIMINATION: DOWN EACH
COLUMN IN TURN, THE ROW WITH THE LARGEST ENTRY IS SWAPPED
INTO PLACE, WHICH CHANGES THE SIGN, AND MULTIPLES OF IT ARE
TAKEN FROM THE ROWS BELOW, WHICH DOES NOT. THE DETERMINANT
IS THEN THE PRODUCT DOWN THE DIAGONAL, WITH THE SIGN. A
COLUMN WITH NOTHING TO SWAP IN GIVES 0: THE MATRIX IS
SINGULAR, AND ⌹ WOULD REFUSE IT.
